 35CL c  1969Ha17: 51-61-MeV {+35}Cl{+5,6+} beams of 80 nA were produced from   
 35CL2c  the Chalk River MP tandem accelerator and bombarded 9.6- mg/cm{+2}     
 35CL3c  carbon. De-excitation |g rays were detected using two 40-cm{+3} Ge(Li) 
 35CL4c  detectors at 125|' and at 0|' or 90|'. Measured E|g, I|g(|q). Deduced  
 35CL5c  levels, mixing ratio, transition strengths, T{-1/2} for 2 levels using 
 35CL6c  the Doppler Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM).                           
 35CL c  1977Sc36: E=53-56 MeV {+35}Cl{+5+} beam of 60 nA produced from a single
 35CL2c  MP Tandem Van de Graaff tandem accelerator at the three-state facility 
 35CL3c  of Brookhaven National Laboratory. Targets of natural Na and Al. A 55  
 35CL4c  cm{+3} coaxial Ge(Li) detector. Measured E|g, I|g(|q). Deduced levels, 
 35CL5c  mixing ratios, transition strengths, T{-1/2} for the levels of 1220,   
 35CL6c  1762 and 2650 keV using the Doppler Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM).   
